From e8cfc579308c41a0b20dae1ade2848455f5873ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deewsing <deewsing@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 10:59:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: skip newidle balance when RT task is runnable

Upstream-Status: Pending

sched_balance_newidle() checks ttwu_pending to bail out early when a
task is pending wakeup via the remote IPI path. However, when an RT
task is woken via the local wakeup path (same CPU), ttwu_pending is
never set. The RT task is directly enqueued onto the local RT runqueue
and need_resched is set, but sched_balance_newidle() has no visibility
into this and proceeds to call sched_balance_update_blocked_averages()
which iterates all CPUs under preempt-disable.

On an 8-core IQ9075-EVK with PREEMPT_RT this causes a 92-153us
preemption-disabled window inside __schedule(), blocking a prio-99
SCHED_FIFO cyclictest thread from running despite need_resched being
set. This is a direct PREEMPT_RT latency violation.

Fix by checking rt.rt_nr_running before entering the expensive load
balancing path. If an RT task is already runnable on this CPU there
is no point pulling more tasks from other CPUs.

The blocked load averages will still be updated by the periodic
nohz_idle_balance() and sched_balance_domains() paths so staleness
is bounded to one scheduler tick.

Fixes: RT latency spikes on IQ9075-EVK (SEAPATH hypervisor port)
Signed-off-by: deewsing <deewsing@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index d9777c81db0d..5b2ae7972568 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -12885,6 +12885,19 @@ static int sched_balance_newidle(struct rq *this_rq, struct rq_flags *rf)
 	if (this_rq->ttwu_pending)
 		return 0;

+	/*
+	 * An RT task was woken directly on this CPU (local wakeup path) and
+	 * is already enqueued on the RT runqueue. ttwu_pending is only set
+	 * for remote IPI wakeups so it won't catch this case. Skip the
+	 * expensive sched_balance_update_blocked_averages() which iterates
+	 * all CPUs under preempt-disable and causes RT latency spikes.
+	 *
+	 * Observed on IQ9075-EVK: 92-153us preemption-disabled window in
+	 * sched_balance_newidle() blocking a prio-99 RT cyclictest thread.
+	 */
+	if (this_rq->rt.rt_nr_running)
+		return 0;
+
 	/*
 	 * We must set idle_stamp _before_ calling sched_balance_rq()
 	 * for CPU_NEWLY_IDLE, such that we measure the this duration
--
